\chapter{Results and Evaluation}

\section{Testing Methodology}

Testing is organised around the end-to-end goal-matching loop: authentication, feed discovery, goal
posting, the request/approval/lobby state machine, trust-and-safety actions, and post-goal rating.

\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.4em]
  \item Functional testing of college-email OTP verification, signup and login.
  \item Feed retrieval, category/date filtering and goal-detail display.
  \item Goal posting, including the auto-accept and anonymous-posting options.
  \item Request-to-join, manual approval/rejection, and auto-accept branches.
  \item Lobby formation once headcount is reached, and in-lobby chat delivery.
  \item Trust-and-safety actions: report, block, gender-preference filtering.
  \item Goal-completion confirmation, no-show flagging and rating capture.
\end{itemize}

